  "notes": "The member's own posts (#1520): the filter chips, the search field, the bulk line, one row's title, meta and trailing group, and the create button. This is the densest page in the account area, and the one a layout review found four defects on by reading alone, so the boxes it must keep are named here before anything measures them. `origin` is the chip row, because the page's frame and the app's frame are different heights and the design is the gaps between these boxes, not where the first one lands. `capture` is the row, the region both clients draw identically and the part that repeats. Two states, because the bulk line is one quiet line with nothing selected and a bordered sticky bar with a selection (#1533): the same boxes are named in both, and the bar's radius, padding and border are measured only in the second, which is where its shape changes on purpose. Widths of the title and the meta run are left out deliberately - they are the run of the words, not a decision. Colours are left out too - they are what the raster proves. The page is the document today (`parity-plan.json` says so, ADR-0178), so the contract is declared here and not under `docs/mobile/visual-gate.json`: the app tags name the boxes a port would draw, and the recording and the pair land with that port, if one is ever drawn (ADR-0118). Until then it is the reviewed target list for the page rather than a gate, which is ADR-0118's #1520 amendment, and the page's own test is what refuses a selector it no longer resolves to.",
